From a145a097ee3f1697cbc5bb2cb546a8fa855cc46a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Davide-F5-Marincione <marincione@di.uniroma1.it>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 00:31:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/21] RR bootstrap: replace the level = totalLimbs -
 currentLimbs identity
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fixes the blocker the previous commit named. EvalBootstrapSetup now succeeds on
an RR chain, along with EvalBootstrapKeyGen and encryption.

THE IDENTITY. OpenFHE's bootstrap derives a ciphertext's level from its limb
count in 17 places:
    SetLevel(L0 - ct.GetNumOfElements())     // level = totalLimbs - currentLimbs
plus two sites where L0 is a LEVEL budget rather than an element count (the ones
feeding lEnc/lDec). The identity holds on a prefix chain and is false under RR by
construction: an RR level is a contiguous WINDOW, and a level drops a variable
number of limbs while adding others back, so limb count does not determine level.
27 levels over 48 limbs.

FIX. RRAwareElementLevel(cryptoParams, elem, L0) recovers the level from the
element's actual MODULI — its first modulus names the window's low edge, which
with the limb count identifies the level uniquely — and throws naming the size
and modulus if no window matches. All 17 sites converted; the two level-budget
L0s become RRNumLevels()-1 under RR.

CLASSIC IS UNCHANGED BY CONSTRUCTION, not merely by test: RRAwareElementLevel's
non-RR branch returns exactly `L0 - elem.GetNumOfElements()`, the expression it
replaced, and every other change is an IsRRChain() ternary or an if/else whose
else-arm is the original code verbatim.

WHERE IT STOPS NOW, and it is a design boundary rather than a bug. With setup
green, EvalBootstrap itself segfaults in PolyImpl::operator*= — a ct*pt multiply
whose operands' limb sets do not line up. The cause is that bootstrap's internals
call the STANDARD scheme ops (EvalMult/ModReduce), which are prefix-chain: they
produce ciphertexts whose limbs are prefixes, while the CtS/StC plaintexts are
now correctly window-shaped. Milestone (b) deferred exactly this on purpose —
"integration with the standard OpenFHE EvalMult/ModReduce paths (RR cts are
driven through RRChain by design)". So a CPU RR bootstrap needs the standard op
path routed through RRChain; that is (b)'s deferred item, not a step-3 defect.

Probe extended (torchfhe tests/rr_bts_setup_probe.cpp) to carry setup -> keygen
-> encrypt -> bootstrap -> precision, and to run the same code path with no RR
chain as a regression check.

Still NOT installed into deps_n32: the shipped OpenFHE is unchanged.
---
 src/pke/lib/scheme/ckksrns/ckksrns-fhe.cpp | 74 ++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 55 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/pke/lib/scheme/ckksrns/ckksrns-fhe.cpp b/src/pke/lib/scheme/ckksrns/ckksrns-fhe.cpp
index b498192a..ae635d3c 100644
--- a/src/pke/lib/scheme/ckksrns/ckksrns-fhe.cpp
+++ b/src/pke/lib/scheme/ckksrns/ckksrns-fhe.cpp
@@ -78,6 +78,36 @@ double GetBigModulus(const std::shared_ptr<lbcrypto::CryptoParametersCKKSRNS> cr
 
 namespace lbcrypto {
 
+// RR (RR_PLAN (c).4c step 3): the LEVEL of a ciphertext element.
+//
+// `level = totalLimbs - currentLimbs` is the prefix-chain identity, and OpenFHE's bootstrap
+// leans on it in 17 places. It is FALSE under RR by construction: an RR level is a contiguous
+// WINDOW of the layout, and a level drops a variable number of limbs while adding others back,
+// so limb count does not determine level. Under RR the level is recovered from the element's
+// actual MODULI — its first modulus names the window's low edge, which together with the limb
+// count identifies the level uniquely. That is a real lookup rather than arithmetic, but it
+// runs once per ciphertext construction in setup/bootstrap, not on any inner loop.
+static uint32_t RRAwareElementLevel(const std::shared_ptr<CryptoParametersCKKSRNS>& cryptoParams,
+                                    const DCRTPoly& elem, uint32_t L0) {
+    if (!cryptoParams->IsRRChain())
+        return L0 - elem.GetNumOfElements();
+
+    const auto& ep      = elem.GetParams()->GetParams();
+    const uint32_t size = static_cast<uint32_t>(ep.size());
+    const uint64_t lowMod = ep[0]->GetModulus().ConvertToInt();
+    const auto& chain   = cryptoParams->GetRRPrimeChain();
+    const uint32_t nLvl = cryptoParams->RRNumLevels();
+    for (uint32_t r = 0; r < nLvl; ++r) {
+        const auto win = cryptoParams->RRWindowAtLevel(nLvl - 1 - r);  // window of RR index r
+        if (win.second - win.first + 1 == size && chain[win.first] == lowMod)
+            return nLvl - 1 - r;
+    }
+    OPENFHE_THROW("RRAwareElementLevel: no RR level has " + std::to_string(size) +
+                  " limbs starting at modulus " + std::to_string(lowMod) +
+                  " — the element is not on any level's window");
+}
