From c3d8258fc8743eeede2e360cd0fdf7fb67fb12f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Davide-F5-Marincione <marincione@di.uniroma1.it>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 00:39:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/21] RR: route ModReduce and EvalMult through RRChain
 (milestone (b) deferred item)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The standard scheme ops are prefix-chain and produce prefix-shaped ciphertexts;
on an RR chain a level is a WINDOW. Milestone (b) deferred this integration on
purpose ("RR cts are driven through RRChain by design"). Bootstrap needs it,
because its internals call the standard ops.

ROUTED (all guarded by IsRRChain(); the classic arm is the original code
verbatim, so prefix chains are unchanged by construction):
- LeveledSHECKKSRNS::ModReduceInternalInPlace -> RRChain::RescaleInPlace, one RR
  level per requested level. The generic body is "DropLastElementAndScale",
  which cannot express an RR transition at all: level r-1's window CONTAINS
  primes level r's does not, so the rescale adds limbs back as well as dropping
  them.
- LeveledSHECKKSRNS::EvalMultInPlace(ct, plaintext) -> EvalMultPlainInPlace.
- LeveledSHECKKSRNS::EvalMult(ct, ct, evk) -> EvalMultRelin. This is a NEW
  override: the base implementation lives in the templated LeveledSHEBase and
  multiplies then calls the generic KeySwitchCore, both of which assume the
  operands are prefixes of one chain and the evk is per-level; under RR the evk
  is a single key at P*Qmax read positionally.

GetRRChain(cc) caches one RRChain per crypto-parameters object. RRChain's
constructor materializes a DCRTPoly::Params per level, so constructing one inside
ModReduce — which runs once per level of every circuit — would have dominated.

Also added a window-mismatch guard to EvalMultPlainInPlace that names both
levels, their limb counts and their low moduli, instead of letting PolyImpl
report a bare "Modulus missmatch". Same reason the RRWindowAtLevel guard paid
off: on an RR chain "same number of limbs" does not mean "same window", so the
bare message cannot distinguish a level error from a window error.

RESULT, probe (torchfhe tests/rr_bts_setup_probe.cpp): setup, keygen, encryption
and now the bootstrap's ModRaise and multiplies all run. It stops further in, and
the backtrace names the next item precisely:

  EvalBootstrap -> EvalRotate -> EvalAtIndex -> EvalAutomorphism
    -> KeySwitchHYBRID::KeySwitchCore -> EvalFastKeySwitchCoreExt -> Times()

i.e. the ROTATION/automorphism keyswitch still goes through the generic HYBRID
implementation. That is the OTHER item (b) deferred verbatim: "rotations/
automorphism RR keyswitch (same KeySwitchCore mechanism, add when (c) needs it)".
RRChain::KeySwitchCore already has the mechanism; it needs wiring to
EvalAutomorphism, plus the automorphism itself applied on the window.

Still NOT installed into deps_n32.
