From 88b64912d6fbc6a186cb8a7073832a74057199a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 02:16:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/21] RR bootstrap: the CtS/StC stage levels were reading `L`
 as a level
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`L` is not a level in either precompute. In the classic arm it is the number of
towers that REMAIN, and the stage level falls out of it:

    towersToDrop = totalTowers - L - d*levelBudget
    level0(CtS)  = towersToDrop + d*(levelBudget-1) = totalTowers - L - d
    level0(StC)  = towersToDrop                     = totalTowers - L - d*levelBudget

The RR arm added in 3c2e65cd used `L + levelBudget - 1` (CtS) and `L` (StC),
i.e. read the remaining-count as an OpenFHE level. Measured consequence, with
the GPU-side diagnostic FIDESLIB_RR_LOAD_DEBUG=1:

  [rr_load] pt: 10 Q-limbs + 13 special -> RR level 5 (window [12,21])
  [rr_lt]   ct level 25 (46 limbs, deg 1) vs pt[0] level 5 (10 limbs) - 15 pts

The CtS plaintexts sat near the chain BOTTOM while the ciphertext arrives from
ModRaise at the TOP, and the ct*pt kernel indexes the plaintext by the
CIPHERTEXT's slot count — so this was an out-of-bounds read, not a wrong result
(compute-sanitizer: "Invalid __global__ read ... at dotProductLtBatchedPt3___,
Access to 0x6000 is out of bounds", blockIdx.y = 11 against a 10-limb plaintext).

The RR analogue is the same expression with towers replaced by LEVELS, since an
RR level is one rescale and the top level index is RRNumLevels()-1. After the fix
the two sides line up level for level and CoeffsToSlots runs to completion:

  [rr_lt] ct level 25 (46 limbs, deg 1) vs pt[0] level 25 (46 limbs)
  [rr_lt] ct level 25 (46 limbs, deg 2) vs pt[0] level 24 (44 limbs)
  [rr_lt] ct level 24 (44 limbs, deg 2) vs pt[0] level 23 (42 limbs)
  [rr_lt] ct level 23 (42 limbs, deg 2) vs pt[0] level 22 (40 limbs)

Classic is untouched: both edits are inside the existing `if (rrChain)` arm.

