RR_BTS_TRACE=1 prints level/limbs/deg/log2(scale) at each bootstrap stage. The
point is that the CLASSIC path is correct and takes the same FLEXIBLEAUTO code,
so the two traces can be diffed and the stage where they stop being structurally
the same IS the bug — no reference implementation needed.

  stage              classic (deg/log2 sf)   RR (deg/log2 sf)
  post-CtS           2 / 54.01               2 / 110.00   ok
  pre-cheby          1 / 27.00               1 /  55.00   ok
  post-cheby         2 / 54.02               2 / 110.05   ok
  post-doubleangle   2 / 54.06               2 / 140.00   <-- +30
  pre-StC            1 / 27.03               1 / 100.00
  post-StC           2 / 54.06               2 / 139.998

RR tracks classic EXACTLY through CoeffsToSlots and the Chebyshev evaluation:
deg-1 carries the region's scaling factor (2^55 in the bootstrap region, against
classic's 2^27) and deg-2 carries its square. So ModRaise, CtS, the plaintext
scales and the Chebyshev evaluator are all consistent.

The divergence is ApplyDoubleAngleIterations: +29.96 bits across R_UNIFORM = 6
iterations, i.e. +4.99 bits PER ITERATION, where classic is flat. Each iteration
is square -> double -> add scalar -> ModReduce, and the level advances by exactly
one per iteration (11 -> 17), so one rescale each. A per-iteration constant of ~5
bits points at the factor that rescale divides by rather than at the arithmetic.

Everything downstream is that drift carried forward: pre-StC reads 100 instead of
~55 and the output lands at 2^100 where its level's table says 2^40, which is the
constant-across-slots decode the probe reports.

