Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 11:09:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 16/21] =?UTF-8?q?RR=20EvalMod:=20a=20128-bit=20shift=20tha?=
 =?UTF-8?q?t=20is=2064-bit=20on=20this=20build=20=E2=80=94=20the=20message?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20flows=20again?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

THE BUG, and it was three lines from where the bracket said it would be:

    double factor = static_cast<uint128_t>(1) << round(log2(qDouble));

At NATIVEINT=32, `uint128_t` is `uint64_t` (basicint.h:57). An RR chain's q0 is
the 3-limb bottom WINDOW, ~2^78, so this shifts by 78 on a 64-bit type: it wraps
to a shift of 14 and `factor` comes out 2^14 instead of 2^78. Measured, side by
side with the working chain:

    classic  pre = 0.999756      qDouble = 2^27.9996
    RR       pre = 1.79189e+19   qDouble = 2^77.9581     <- exactly 2^63.96

`pre` feeds `scaleEnc`, which is the scale the CtS PLAINTEXTS are encoded at — so
CoeffsToSlots was multiplying by a factor 2^64 wrong and destroying the message,
while every stage around it measured correct. A classic chain never trips it
because its q0 is 2^28 and a shift of 28 is fine. Computing the power in double
(std::pow) fixes it.

SECOND, uncovered by the first: the integer 2^deg recovery after the Chebyshev.
COMPOSITESCALING already skips it because it uses the sf/q0 input normalization
and carries the matching recovery in the StC plaintexts as scaleDec = q0/sf(0).
RR uses the same convention, so applying 2^deg on top double-counts it — visible
as a jump of exactly 8.4e6 = 2^23 = 2^deg between post-doubleangle and pre-StC,
where classic's deg = 1 makes the same multiply harmless.

RESULT: the message now flows through the whole of EvalMod with
classic-comparable magnitudes, where before every stage past CtS was a constant.

    post-CtS          0.00682  0.01223  -0.03305   (was ~1e-6)
    pre-cheby        -0.06071  0.03035   0.06071
    post-cheby        0.32980 -0.25794   0.48469   (was 0.779474 constant)
    post-doubleangle -0.04087  0.02800  -0.05601
    pre-StC          -0.04087  0.02800  -0.05601   (2^deg no longer double-counted)

STILL FAILING at StC: post-StC does not decrypt, and the output scale is 2^107.2
at a level whose table says 2^55.9. That is the one remaining stage, and the
suspect is the StC plaintext scale (scaleDec and MakeAuxPlaintext's boundary
gating), not the pipeline feeding it.

Gates: rr_cpu_gate PASS on both chains; classic control PASS at 13.5 bits.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012CioZybBn4CVXK46MgRWfL
